  {
   "h": "70 to 100: a little math",
   "body": [
    "French in France and Quebec has no single word for 70, 80 or 90. 70 is *soixante-dix* (sixty-ten), so 71 is *soixante et onze*, 75 is *soixante-quinze*.",
    "80 is *quatre-vingts* (four twenties), with an s only when nothing follows. 81 is *quatre-vingt-un* (no *et*). 90 is *quatre-vingt-dix* (four twenties + ten), so 99 is *quatre-vingt-dix-neuf*. 100 is *cent*."
   ],
